                <pb facs="0161" n="73" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg73"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.5151/202: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-20T17:00:00-05:00">December 20, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>110. 1. Reply is urgently desired to the Department’s 106, December 13, 5
                    p.m.</p>
                <p>2. Advise in particular, so that we hear by tomorrow forenoon if possible,
                    whether it is true that exchange is to be supplied for raw material imports only
                    and, if so, the effect on imports of wheat flour.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
